<article class="env-lemma" id="09UG">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/09UG">Lemma <span data-tag="09UG">36.12.4</span>.</a> Let $\{ f_ i : X_ i \to X\} $ be an fpqc covering of schemes. Let $E \in D(\mathcal{O}_ X)$. Then $E$ is perfect if and only if each $Lf_ i^*E$ is perfect. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Pullback always preserves perfect complexes, see Cohomology, Lemma <a href="/tag/09UA" data-tag="09UA">20.49.6</a>. Conversely, assume that $Lf_ i^*E$ is perfect for all $i$. Then the cohomology sheaves of each $Lf_ i^*E$ are quasi-coherent, see Lemma <a href="/tag/08E5" data-tag="08E5">36.10.1</a> and Cohomology, Lemma <a href="/tag/08CQ" data-tag="08CQ">20.49.5</a>. Since the morphisms $f_ i$ is flat we see that $H^ p(Lf_ i^*E) = f_ i^*H^ p(E)$. Thus the cohomology sheaves of $E$ are quasi-coherent by Descent, Proposition <a href="/tag/023T" data-tag="023T">35.5.2</a>. Having said this the lemma follows formally from Cohomology, Lemma <a href="/tag/08CQ" data-tag="08CQ">20.49.5</a> and Lemmas <a href="/tag/09UD" data-tag="09UD">36.12.1</a> and <a href="/tag/09UE" data-tag="09UE">36.12.2</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>